            Group(null, 0, listOf(
                Item("Robo", R.drawable.pet1, "A Round Robot With Cat-Like Ears? Besides Its Bizarre Look, This Pet Is Useful For Players Who Are Master Gloo Wall Users. Its Wall Enforcement Skill Creates A Protective Shield On The Gloo Wall And Gives It An Extra HP Buff, Making It Harder To Destroy.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Wall Enforcement")),
                Item("Spirit Fox", R.drawable.pet2, "This Cute Little Fox Uses The Well Fed Ability, Which Increases The Amount Of HP Earned From Healing Items By 10. That Extra Bump In Health Can Be Exactly What You Need To Stay In The Fight. Spirit Fox Is Also One Of The First Pets You Can Unlock, So It Makes A Great Starting Option.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Well Fed")),
                Item("Mr. Waggor", R.drawable.pet3, "The Latest Addition To The FFF Pack Is This Cool Penguin With The Smooth Gloo Ability. Mr Waggor Can Produce An Additional Gloo Wall Grenade Every 120/100/100 Seconds. Comes In Handy During Desperate, Late Game Decisions.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Smooth Gloo")),
                Item("Falco", R.drawable.pet4, "Falco In FFF Is A Pet That Has The Skill Of Skyline Spree. This skill Is Probably One Of The Best Pet Skills To Have In A Battle Royale Squad Game. Skyline Spree Is A Pet Skill That Increases The Diving And Gliding Speed Of The User And All The Teammates When You Jump Out Of The Airplane.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Skyline Spree")),
                Item("Ottero", R.drawable.pet5, "With Double Blubber, The Otter-Inspired Pet Will Give Players A Bonus EP Whenever They Use A Recovery Item. This Bonus EP Starts At 35-Percent Of HP Healed And Grows To Up To 65-Percent As They Level Up. This Can Become A Life-Saver In Longer Excursions, As Players Need All The EP They Can Have For Emergency Heals.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Double Blubber")),
                Item("Dreki", R.drawable.pet6, "Mythology Describes Dragons As Fearsome Creatures, Often Forcing Others To Cower In Fear In Their Presence And Making It Easier For Dragons To Hunt Them Down. The Pet Dreki Has Somewhat The Same Property, Allowing Players To Spot Opponents Quickly And Catch Them While They're Trying To Recover.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Dragon Glare")),
                Item("Night Panther", R.drawable.pet7, "Night Panther Has Probably One Of The Most Basic Skills. The Skill Is Called Weight Training And What It Does Is Increase Inventory Space. Using This Pet's Skill Will Increase Your Inventory Space By 45 At The Max Level. A Skill Like This One Is Basically Useless In The Clash Squad Game Mode As Your Inventory Space Is Not Even Used At All.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Weight Training")),
                Item("Detective Panda", R.drawable.pet8, "This skill is called Panda's Blessings, And It Will Restore 10 HP To Its User After Every Kill. Clash Squad Games Get Intense In The Upper Ranks And Fights Are Happening All Over The Small Map. Many Players Who May Not Have Unlocked All The Character Skills Tend To Use Passive Skills Like Jota's Sustained Raids, And Luqueta's Hat Trick To Keep Up Their HP I The Game.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Panda's Blessings")),
                Item("Kactus", R.drawable.pet9, "Kactus Is A Cute-Looking Companion Having Horns And Hands Similar To Cactuses. However, There Is No Information About The Release Date Of The New Pet. Most Probably, Developers Will Introduce A S Top-Up Event After The Arrival Of The OB38 Update From Where Kactus Can Be Collected.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Self-Sufficient")),
                Item("Fang", R.drawable.pet10, "Fang Has An Eye-Catching Appearance And Will Be Loved By Many For Sure. It Can Provide HP To The Owner Whenever Their Teammates Get Knocked Out. There Are Different Levels Of Ability And Players Will Have To Upgrade Fang To Unlock Those. The Level 1 Ability Unlocks At The Pet's Base Level Whereas The Level 3 Ability Unlocks When The Pet Is At Level 7.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Wolf Pact")),
                Item("Hoot", R.drawable.pet11, "Hoot Has A Unique Ability Called 'Far-Sighted'. It Has No Skill To Cool Down. Hoot Can Increase The Range And Time Duration Of Scanning Items And Skills. However, The Skill Can Be Upgraded To Use It To The Fullest. While Using A Level 3 Hoot, The Owner Can Reach An Added Range Of 10m And The Scan Duration Will Last For An Extra 2.5 s. Moreover, The Results Can Be Shared With Teammates.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Far-sighted")),
                Item("Arvon", R.drawable.pet12, "It Can Detect The Exact Number Of Enemies In An Area Of 50m, Irrespective Of Their Position. However The Effect Lasts For Only Three Seconds, And Results Are Shared With Teammates. In Level 1, Players Can Use This Skill For One Time Only. The Skill Will Last For Six Seconds At The Highest Level And Can Be Used Thrice Per Match.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Dinoculars")),
                Item("Zasil", R.drawable.pet13, "Zasil Possesses A Unique Ability That Increases The Recovered Health Of The User. It Can Be Done If The Player Uses An Inhaler, Medical Kit, Or Repair kit. Zasil's Skill Is Not Of Much Importance. The Pet Seems To Be Of No Particular Advantage Than Just Increasing The Number Of Pets In FFF By One.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Extra Luck")),
                Item("Finn", R.drawable.pet14, "By Looking At The Leaked Images One Can Easily Understand That The Upcoming Pet In FFF Is Inspired By Sharks. Finn's Description Reads, \"Dare To Challenge Me For A Swim?\" In The FFF OB34 Advanced Server.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Dash Splash")),
                Item("Agent Hop", R.drawable.pet15, "Players can't Stay In A Single Area For Too Long In A Battle Royale, Especially Since The Safe Zone Shrinks The Longer They Stay In The Battle. As Such, Players Will Inevitably Face Other Characters Or Risk Getting Damaged If They Remain In The Zone. With Agent Hop, Players Get More Incentive To Explore Within The Zone And Prepare For Enemy Encounters.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Bouncing Bonus")),
                Item("Yeti", R.drawable.pet16, "Yeti Has Skills That Can Reduce Damage From Explosions Such As Grenades And Grenade Launchers, Making It Very Suitable For Use In The Currently Popular Meta Grenade. Yeti Can Be The Toughest Counter For Beaston And Alvaro.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Frost Fortress")),
                Item("Flash", R.drawable.pet17, "The Flash Pet Will Also Provide A Buff To The Players By His Special Ability Called \"Steel Shell\". Flash Can Reduce The Damage From Bullets And Knives From Behind By 10%. But There Is A 100 Points Durability, Which Cooldowns For 150 Seconds. However, Flash Can Be Upgraded To Its Ultimate Form To Reduce Damage By 25% Up Until 150 Durability Points. At This Stage, The Cooldown Will Reduce To 90 Seconds.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Steel Shell")),
                Item("Moony", R.drawable.pet18, "Moony's Special Ability Reduces The Damage Taken While The Character Is Using The Healing Items. In Simple Words, If The Character Is Using Medical Kits, Inhaler, And Even Healing Pistols, The Damage Suffered While The Process Would Be Less.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Paranormal Protection")),
                Item("Dr. Beanie", R.drawable.pet19, "It Basically Increases The Movement Speed If The Character Is Walking Like A Duck. The Pet Will Be A Perfect Option For The Players Who Love To Use LMG Machine Guns Such As KORD. Because Machine Guns Provide The Best Performance In The Rouch Position And The Duck Helps Players Increasing Their Movement Speed In This Position.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Dashy Duckwalk")),
                Item("Sensei Tig", R.drawable.pet20, "Spotting Opponents Quickly Is What Often Separates A Survivor And A Dead Body In A Gunfight, And Man-Marking Is A Viable Strategy To Do Through Man-Marking, Players Can Spot Players In A Vicinity Through Certain Skills. However, Players Who Have Sensei Tig With Them Can Rely On The Power Of Stealth To Disable These Advantages.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Nimble Ninja")),
                Item("Pug", R.drawable.pet21, "The Only Major Flaw Of The Pet Is That It Doesn't Have Any Skills. Either Active Or Passive Pug Does Not Come With A Skill. However, Players Can Still Use Other Pets' Abilities While Equipping Pugs. The Pug Is A Beautiful Pet Having A Cool Suit And Basic Skin. Since It Doesn't Have Any Skills, Players May Get It For Free From Some Simple Missions.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "No skill")),
                Item("Shiba", R.drawable.pet22, "This Pet Has The Skill Of Mushroom Sense, And As The Name Implies, It Only Is Good For Mushrooms. In The Battle Royale Games, Mushrooms Restore The EP Of A Player When Consumed. Shiba's Skill Allows It To Mark A Mushroom On The Mini-Map For A Few Seconds. A Pet Skill Like Mushroom Sense Is Useful In Battle Royale Games But Will Be A Waste In Clash Squad Games.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Mushroom Sense")),
                Item("Beaston", R.drawable.pet23, "As The Name Suggests, Beaston's Skill Gives Its User A Beast-Like Strength To Throw Utility. Its Skill Is Called Helping Hands, And It Increases The Throwing Range Of Flashbangs, Grenades, Gloo Walls, And Smokes By 30% At Its Max Level. Even Though This Pet's Skill Can Be Used In Both Battle Royale Games And In Clash Squads, It Is More Used In The Latter Game Mode. The Reason For That Is The Frequency At Which Players Are Throwing Grenades. In The Higher-Ranked Lobbies Of Clash Squad, You Will See That Players Start Using Utility Like Gloo Walls And Grenades Fairly Early.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Helping Hand")),
                Item("Rockie", R.drawable.pet24, "This Is A Pet That Is Mostly Used By Players Who Have The Time Turner Active Skill. Rockie Is Probably One Of The Most Used Pets In FFF By Players Who Have Active Skills. Rockie's Skill Is Called Stay Chill And What It Does Is Decrease The Cooldown Time Of An Active Skill By 15%. This Is Why Most Of The Players Who Are Using Chrono's Time Turner Skill Use Rockie As A Pet.", listOf(R.string.stat_ability to "Stay Chill")),
            )),
        ))
    }
    val VEHICLES: Section by lazy {
        Section(R.string.cat_vehicles, listOf(
            Group(null, 0, listOf(
                Item("Sports Car", R.drawable.sportcar, "The Sports Car Is Probably The Best Looking Vehicle In The Game - and Also The Fastest. It Can Carry Up To 2 Players. Overall, This Car Is One Of The Top Choices You Could Get In A Solo Match - It Unrivaled Speed Could Help You Rotate To Literally Anywhere On The Map Without Fail. The Fact That It Can Reach Top Speed Faster Would Also Increase The Damage It Deals When You Crash Into People.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "400", R.string.stat_acceleration to "4600", R.string.stat_control to "20", R.string.stat_speed to "80")),
                Item("Monstar Car", R.drawable.monstarcar, "An AirDrop Only Vehicle That Can Carry Up To 4 Players. The Monster Truck Has High Armor, HP And Can Travel Difficult Terrains With It's 8000 Acceleration Stats. It Top Speed Is Pretty Low, However.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "800", R.string.stat_acceleration to "8000", R.string.stat_control to "15", R.string.stat_speed to "45")),
                Item("Tuk Tuk", R.drawable.tuktuk, "A Weird 3 Wheels Bike That can Carry Up To Three Players - It Is Pretty Much The Weakest Vehicle In The Game, With The Lowest Stat On All 4 Attributes. 3 People Can Fit On It So There's That.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "300", R.string.stat_acceleration to "1200", R.string.stat_control to "15", R.string.stat_speed to "35")),
                Item("Motor Cycle", R.drawable.motorcycle, "A Great Solo Vehicle - It Has The Best Control In The Game And You Can Change Direction Rapidly Anytime You Want. The Motorcycle's Top Speed Is 60, Which Makes It The Second Fastest Vehicle On The Map - It Would Take You Quite A While To Get To That Speed, However As The Acceleration Stat Is Rather Low. The Size Also Allows The Bike To Travel Through Narrow Areas.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "300", R.string.stat_acceleration to "1500", R.string.stat_control to "40", R.string.stat_speed to "60")),
                Item("AmBhiBlan", R.drawable.ambhiblan, "A Vehicle With Low General Stats In Exchange For The Ability To Travel On Both Land And Water - It Can Carry 2 Players. Overall, You Can Use This To Cross Water Regions Without Having To Use Bridges - However, It's Best To Ditch This Vehicle For Another As Soon As Possible.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "300", R.string.stat_acceleration to "1400", R.string.stat_control to "15", R.string.stat_speed to "40")),
                Item("Military Jeep", R.drawable.jeep, "An Upgrade Over The Pickup Truck. The Jeep Has Decent Protection And Can Carry A Whole Team - The Third Best Vehicle On The Map. It Is Somewhat Slower Than The Pickup Truck, However.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "500", R.string.stat_acceleration to "2900", R.string.stat_control to "15", R.string.stat_speed to "40")),
                Item("Van", R.drawable.van, "This Is The Default Vehicle In Garena FFF - It Is An All-Rounder Type Of Car With Decent Stats. Seats 2 People. A Solid Choice For Solo Players.", listOf(R.string.stat_hp to "400", R.string.stat_acceleration to "2100", R.string.stat_control to "12", R.string.stat_speed to "55")),
            )),
        ))
    }
    val MAPS: Section by lazy {
        Section(R.string.tool_maps, listOf(
            Group("Next Tera", R.drawable.nextera, listOf(
                Item("Intellect Center", R.drawable.nt1, "A Research Area With A Number Of Small Buildings And Great Loot All Over. It Is Connected To The Main Island By Three Bridges."),
                Item("Twin Bridge", R.drawable.nt2, "This Spot Has Two Gigantic Bridges That Players Can Land On Top. Overall, Twin Bridge Is A Transition Area That Is Unlikely To See Much Traffic."),
                Item("Museum", R.drawable.nt3, "A Futuristic Showroom With A Lot Of Platforms, Hallways And Hiding Spots. There Is A Decent Quantity Of Loot Placed Strategically In The Main Building."),
                Item("Mortar Ruins", R.drawable.nt4, "This Area Is Filled With Broken Ruins As Far As The Eye Can See. Overall, It Is Also A Dangerous Area To Be In - There Is Not Much Cover Left And Players Are Constantly Exposed In The Open."),
                Item("Turbine", R.drawable.nt5, "This Is A Special Area Filled With Gigantic Turbines. Overall, The Turbines Are Just Decorations And The Drops Of The Location Are Rather Poor. It Is Also Separated From The Main Island By Water."),
                Item("Farmtopia", R.drawable.nt6, "Farmtopia Is A Futuristic Farm That Covers The Entire Center Of The Map. Due To Its Location, A Lot Of Players Would Land Here And Fight Right From The Start."),
                Item("Zipway", R.drawable.nt7, "The Zipway Is A Transition Area Right Next To Farmtopia In The Middle Of The Map. However, Unlike Farmtopia, It Has No Big Buildings And Therefore Doesn't Have Any Good Loot."),
                Item("Rust Town", R.drawable.nt8, "Rust Town Is More Or Less A Continuation Of The Mortar Ruins, But Unlike The Ruins, It Is Intact And Has Buildings Filled With Loot."),
                Item("Grav Labs", R.drawable.nt9, "Grav Labs Contain The Previously Mentioned Anti-Gravity Area. It Is A Research Factory Of Anti-Gravity. Players Who Land Here Will Get The Chance To Participate In Airborne Gunfights."),
                Item("Deca Square", R.drawable.nt10, "Deca Square Is A Huge Open Area Filled With Buildings And Shops. The Most Notable Thing About This Location Is That It Is Surrounded By Pink Flower Fields."),
                Item("Plazaria", R.drawable.nt11, "Plazaria Is A Huge Fast Food Restaurant That Players Can Check Out. It Is Near The Center Of The Map, Right Next To Deca Square."),
                Item("Boxing Gym", R.drawable.nt12, "Boxing Gym Area Is A Popular Location That Players Can Visit During Matches. It Is Usually Recognized By It's Distinctive Appearance Featuring Boxing Rings, Training Equipment, And Often A Theme Reflecting An Actual Boxing Training Facility."),
                Item("Mud Site", R.drawable.nt13, "Contrary To It's Name, Mud Site Is An Uncompleted Building Area That Has Barely Any Mud. There Are A Lot Of Small Buildings That Players Can Clear Out For Loot."),
            )),
            Group("Alpine", R.drawable.alpine, listOf(
                Item("SnowFall", R.drawable.alp1, "Snowfall Has A Lot Of Snowy Terrains, So It Is Arguably The Most Popular Location On The Alpine Map. Since The Area Has A Lot Of Snow, You Can Easily Find Loot Lying Around Or Even Hide Easily Behind The Structures During Combat."),
                Item("Vantage", R.drawable.alp2, "Vantage Gym Is A Dynamic Location In FFF That Offers Both Challenges And Opportunities For Players Who Choose To Land There. It's A Place Where Quick Decision-Making And Sharp Shooting Skills Are Often Put To The Test."),
                Item("Rail Road", R.drawable.alp3, "The \"Railroad\" Area Refers To A Location On The Bermuda Map. This Area Is Situated Near The Center Of The Map, Typically Marked By A Railway Track And Several Train Carriages."),
                Item("Dock", R.drawable.alp4, "The Dock Area Is A Popular Landing Spot On The Bermuda Map. It's Located In The Southwestern Part Of The Map And Is Characterized By It's Numerous Shipping Containers, Warehouses And Cargo Ships."),
                Item("River Mouth", R.drawable.alp5, "River Mouth Is A Location On The Bermuda Map. It's One Of The Many Points Of Interest Where Players Can Land And Loot For Weapons, Items, And Supplies, Featuring Several Riverside Buildings."),
                Item("Fusion", R.drawable.alp6, "The \"Fusion\" Feature Allows Players To Combine Duplicate Items To Obtain Higher-Tier Items Or Exclusive Rewards. The Fusion Area Adds Depth To The Game's Customization Options."),
            )),
            Group("Bermuda", R.drawable.bermuda, listOf(
                Item("Hanger", R.drawable.br1, "The \"Hanger\" Area Is One Of The Locations On The Bermuda Map. It's Typically A Medium-Sized Compound With Various Buildings, Containers, And Structures, Offering A Mix Of Close-Quarters Combat And Loot."),
                Item("Peak", R.drawable.br2, "Being The Core Sector In Bermuda Map, Peak Has Always Been The Hottest Spot That Many Players Choose To Drop In. Apart From The Most Valuable Items, The Peak Also Offers A Clear View Of The Entire Island Thanks To It's Height."),
                Item("Rim Nam Village", R.drawable.br3, "Rim Nam Village Is Inspired By The Famous Holiday Spot Maldives. It Is Located On The Far Left Of The Bermuda Map, Composed Of Several Houses In The Water Linked By Small Wooden Bridges."),
                Item("Clock Tower", R.drawable.br4, "The Clock Tower Area In FFF Is A Dynamic And Challenging Location That Provides Both Opportunities And Risks For Players. Mastering The Strategies Specific To This Area Can Improve Your Chances Of Survival."),
                Item("Mars Electric", R.drawable.br5, "It Is Possible That This Is The Center Of Electricity In Bermuda Map - There Are 2 Nuclear Reactors And Several Warehouses."),
                Item("Factory", R.drawable.br6, "There Is An Old Unused Factory Here. This Is One Of The Busiest Places, As An Average Of 20% Of Players Drop Here. It Is Impossible To Reach The Top Of The Factory Except From The Start."),
                Item("Cap Town", R.drawable.br7, "Cape Town Is The Capital Of South Africa; The Buildings Here Are Also Similar To The Original In Africa. Mainly Shotguns And Sub-Machine Guns Can Be Found Here."),
                Item("GraveYard", R.drawable.br8, "Graveyard Refers To A Cemetery. This Is One Of The Most Notable Places On The Bermuda Map Because Of A Few Tombstones Right Next To The Mansion. The Architecture Resembles A Small Village In Norfolk, England."),
                Item("ShipYard", R.drawable.br9, "The Shipyard Is One Of The Popular Locations On The Bermuda Map, Known For It's Unique Layout And Strategic Advantages. It Offers A Mix Of Risk And Reward With Valuable Loot."),
            )),
            Group("Bermuda Remastered", R.drawable.bermuda2, listOf(
                Item("Hanger", R.drawable.brr1, "\"Hangar\" Is One Of The Many Locations Where Players Can Drop And Find Loot, Engage In Combat, And Strategize For Survival."),
                Item("Observatory", R.drawable.brr2, "The Observatory Is Situated On Elevated Terrain, Providing A Tactical Advantage For Snipers And Players Who Prefer Long-Range Combat. From This Vantage Point You Can Easily Spot Enemies Approaching From Lower Ground."),
                Item("Academy", R.drawable.brr3, "The Academy Is A Prime Location For Players Looking To Start With High-Tier Loot And Engage In Early Battles. Mastering This Area Involves Quick Looting, Strategic Positioning, And Effective Team Communication."),
                Item("Nurek Dam", R.drawable.brr4, "Located On The North Of The Island Is The Nurek Dam, Which Replaced The Plantation And Riverside In The Previous Version. This Place Provides Green Energy For The Whole Island And Is A Great Place To Camp."),
                Item("Mill", R.drawable.brr5, "Mill Is One Of The Best Locations On The FFF Bermuda Map To Find Good Loot. Even Though The Buildings Are Limited, The Location Has A Lot For You."),
                Item("The Circuit", R.drawable.brr6, "The Circuit Is Typically Located On One Of The Game's Maps. Landing In The Circuit Can Be Advantageous Due To It's Loot But Can Also Be Risky As It Might Be A Popular Landing Spot."),
                Item("Samurai's Garden", R.drawable.brr7, "Among The Four Newly Added Locations, Samurai's Garden Is Likely The Hottest Spot Thanks To The Hidden Story Behind It. The Isolated Island Is The Abandoned Estate Of The Hayato Family, With A Japanese-Style Temple Surrounded By Cherry Blossom Trees And A Zen Garden."),
            )),
            Group("Kalahari", R.drawable.kalahari, listOf(
                Item("Shrines", R.drawable.kala1, "The First Location With The Best Loot Rate Is Shrines. This Ancient Ruins Can Be Used As A Hiding Place For Guerilla Tactics. Besides Looting, You Can Set Traps To Take Out Incoming Enemies."),
                Item("Council Hall", R.drawable.kala2, "Council Hall Is Built By The Community Leaders In Kalahari. There's A Platform Used For Meetings. Although The Map Is Quite Small, Council Hall Has High-Tier Loot Items."),
                Item("Bay Front", R.drawable.kala3, "BayFront Is Considered Among The Top Landing Spots By The Community. It Is Quite Popular And Encompasses A Large Amount Of Land Populated With A Great Number Of Structures, With Enough Loot To Last The Entire Match."),
                Item("Refinery", R.drawable.kala4, "The Refinery Is One Of The Most Popular Places To Land And Can Be Considered The Best Place To Loot. Plenty Of Ammo And Weaponry Is Scattered All Over. There's A ZipLine And An Armor Upgrade Kit Nearby As Well."),
                Item("Santa Catarina", R.drawable.kala5, "Another Unique Place In This Map - A Wrecked Vessel. There's A Good Hiding Spot Below The Vessel's Floor In The Captain's Cabin. Enough Resources Are Available For The Initial Stages Of The Game."),
                Item("Command Post", R.drawable.kala6, "In This Place You're Bound To Engage In Battle Real Soon, But That Doesn't Stop Players From Landing Here Because Of The Heavy Loot Scattered Around The Houses And Tents. An Armor Upgrade Kit Is Available Too."),
                Item("Mammoth", R.drawable.kala7, "Mammoth Has A Massive Skeleton That Reaches Up High And Is Said To Hold A Hidden Mystery. You Can Get Decent Items And Equipment Here, But Because The Map Is Wide Open You Are Prone To Being Targeted."),
                Item("Confinement", R.drawable.kala8, "A Prison For All The Criminals. This Location Has A Lot Of Rooms That You Can Use For Ambushing Your Enemies."),
            )),
            Group("Purgatory", R.drawable.purgatory, listOf(
                Item("Forge", R.drawable.pu1, "Forge Is A Less Crowded Location On Even Terrain Containing High Tier Loot. It Contains A Gigantic Warehouse With A Crane. However, There Isn't Much Cover Aside From A Few Containers."),
                Item("Ski Lodge", R.drawable.pu2, "The Ski Lodge Is A Crowded Location On High Terrain Containing High Tier Loot, Representing An Actual Ski Lodge Going Straight From Up-To Downhill. The Area Is Almost Completely Open-Space."),
                Item("Lumber Mill", R.drawable.pu3, "Lumber Mill Is A Location On Even Terrain Containing Mediocre Loot. The Area Around The Location Does Not Provide Much Protection Except For A Few Trees And Trailers."),
                Item("Central", R.drawable.pu4, "Central Is A Location On Even Terrain Containing Mediocre Loot. It Has A Few Houses, Some With Over 3 Floors And Climbable Roofs. It Is Also A Good Camping Spot Providing Much Cover Between It's Walls."),
                Item("Golf Course", R.drawable.pu5, "Golf Course Is A Less Crowded Location On Even Terrain Containing Low Tier Loot, Characterized By It's Open Field With A Stadium. One Of The Least Passed By Areas Due To Little To No Cover."),
                Item("Mt. Villa", R.drawable.pu6, "Mt. Villa Is A Less Crowded Location On High Terrain Containing Low Tier Loot. A Unique Uphill Location With A Lighthouse And Houses Surrounded By Trees - Good For Camping While Scouting Downhill Enemies."),
                Item("Moathouse", R.drawable.pu7, "Moathouse Is A Highly Crowded Location On Low Terrain Containing High Tier Loot. A Unique Location With 3 Structures Reached By Swimming Or Zip Lines. It Has Good Cover Unless Swimming In The Open Waters."),
            )),
        ))
    }
    val TIPS: List<Article> by lazy {
        listOf(
            Article("Choose Correct Landing Points", "Pick an isolated spot near a town.", "Choosing a landing point is the first step to victory. Although it seems trivial, it isn't — deciding where to start the game matters. Pick a place that's isolated from other players, close to a city but not right in the middle of it. The best option is to glide over the town, watch where other people land, and then drop in to explore. Don't expose yourself too much before you have the proper equipment, especially in busy areas where many players gather."),
            Article("Gear Up After Landing", "Grab weapons, armour and med-kits fast.", "Once you land, the first thing to do is find weapons, protection, first-aid kits, and similar items. At the beginning of the game, grab everything you can — you can always improve and replace your equipment later."),
            Article("Explore Military Sites", "Watchtowers and tents hold great loot.", "If there's no enemy in sight, explore points of interest such as watchtowers, containers, and military tents — they usually hold a lot of loot. It's risky to explore these areas at the very start, but in the mid-game there's plenty to grab with fewer players lurking. These spots often contain kits to upgrade your bulletproof vest, so upgrade as soon as possible — the last players standing always have powerful weapons."),
            Article("Pay Attention To The Safe Zone", "Stay inside the circle to avoid the storm.", "The safe area is shown by a circle on the map and mini-map. Inside it you're safe; outside, the radioactive storm drains your health over time. Watch the safe zone closely — you'll often see players rushing to escape the storm before it's too late, which is a great opportunity to eliminate opponents."),
            Article("Look At The Mini Map", "Read sounds, drones and danger zones.", "The mini-map helps you avoid many threats. If you hear gunshots nearby, look for the red triangles that show where they came from, so you know enemies are close. Explosions and player-driven vehicles appear as yellow or red dots, telling you which direction sounds come from. Red circles mark hazardous bombing areas — leave them quickly. A yellow circle means a drone is exposing player positions, so stay out of it."),
            Article("Take Cover", "Use the environment to stay protected.", "Buildings, walls, containers, stones, and trees are everywhere on the map — use them as cover. The worst thing you can do is stay exposed. While moving, use the environment for protection. Still, proceed with caution: you never know when an enemy is waiting behind a wall, ready to take you out."),
            Article("Use The Vehicle Carefully", "Move fast, but vehicles are loud.", "Vehicles let you move quickly to loot-rich areas and can run past players on the road. But they're loud — other players can hear you coming. Use cars, trucks, and motorcycles carefully so you don't reveal your location."),
        )
    }
    val DIAMOND_TIPS: List<Article> by lazy {
        listOf(
            Article("Beginners Guide", "", "\n\n".let { sep -> listOf("If you're new to battle royale games, you might wonder how they work. While FFF has a number of modes, the one you'll spend the most time in is the standard Battle Royale mode.", "FFF has a large roster of unique characters, each with their own special ability. Characters can equip abilities from others to create a build. Some skills boost stats in battle, while active skills give a temporary advantage.", "FFF has a huge collection of weapons found from random loot drops. Each category has strengths and drawbacks — shotguns shine in short-range fights, while others perform better at long range.", "Unlike many battle royale games, FFF has several maps. Each has a unique layout and landmarks with loot. Ranked gives random maps, but certain playlists let you choose specific ones.", "FFF has a Ranked mode to try once you're familiar with the game. You gain points to climb the leaderboards — the better you play and the more you win, the higher your rank.", "As a mobile FPS, you won't aim with a controller or keyboard and mouse. Finding the perfect settings is trial and error, but tuning key settings improves your aim.", "Choosing a landing point is the first step to victory. Pick a spot isolated from others, near a town but not too close. Glide over, watch where others land, then drop in to explore.", "Once you land, find weapons, protection, and first-aid kits. At the start, grab everything you can — you can always improve and replace equipment later.", "If no enemy is in sight, explore watchtowers, containers, and military tents — they usually hold lots of loot, including vest upgrades. Upgrade as soon as possible.", "The safe area is shown by a circle on the map and mini-map. Inside it you're safe; outside, the storm drains your health. Players fleeing the storm make easy targets.", "Use the mini-map to spot threats: red triangles show gunshot origins, yellow/red dots show explosions and vehicles, red circles mark bombing zones, and a yellow circle means a drone is exposing positions.", "Buildings, walls, containers, stones, and trees are everywhere — use them as cover. Never stay exposed, but stay cautious; an enemy could be waiting behind any wall.", "Vehicles move you quickly to loot-rich areas, but they're loud. Use cars, trucks, and motorcycles carefully so you don't reveal your location.", "Tinker with the different settings to improve aim accuracy. The best way to find your perfect setup is to experiment yourself.", "Training mode helps you master your settings. Practise combat in the Combat Zone, where you fight other users in an FFA arena.").joinToString(sep) }),
            Article("Rank Increase Tips", "", "\n\n".let { sep -> listOf("Your game's outcome can depend on where you land. Crowded areas mean early fights where you may be at a disadvantage; a quieter spot gives time to gather supplies.", "Your top priority after landing is collecting loot — weapons, ammo, armor, and medical supplies. The better your gear, the higher your odds of survival.", "Playing with a squad dramatically increases your chances. A team helps take on enemies faster, provides cover fire, and can revive you if you're knocked out.", "The circle is crucial. As it shrinks, move closer to the center. Staying outside deals damage that can kill you over time.", "Use cover for a tactical advantage and protection from enemy fire. FFF has many kinds of cover, such as structures, trees, and rocks.", "A rank push demands practice. The more you play, the better you get and the more techniques you'll learn.", "Every weapon has unique strengths and weaknesses. Pick the right weapon for your playstyle — shotguns and SMGs for close quarters, snipers or rifles for range — and mind the attachments.", "You never know when an enemy hides behind a corner. Stay alert and aware; audio cues let you hear enemy footsteps and gunshots.", "Grenades are very effective — damaging vehicles or flushing enemies out of cover. FFF has frag grenades, smoke grenades, and Gloo Walls.", "Complete daily missions and events to earn diamonds and experience. Check the game's events and quests regularly to push your rank faster.").joinToString(sep) }),
            Article("HeadShot Tips", "", "\n\n".let { sep -> listOf("Open Settings and adjust two crucial values for headshots. Recommended sensitivity: General 90-100, Red Dot 90-100, 2x Scope 90-100, 4x Scope 90-100, Sniper Scope 40-50, Free Look 90-100.", "Controls: Aim Precision = Default, Left Fire Button = Always, Quick Weapon Switch = On, Quick Reload = Off, Reload Progress on Crosshair = Off, Free Look = On, Hold Fire to Scope = On, Grenade Slot = Double, Vehicle Controls = Two-handed, Auto-Parachute = On, Run Mode = Classic.", "Avoid changing the primary layout — it jumbles gameplay and confuses you. You can still customise some controls, like a 4-finger claw layout that suits your playstyle.", "In Settings, enable the precise-aim option in the Controls tab. This turns off the automatic assistance that makes landing headshots harder.", "Crosshair position matters. Keep it slightly above the enemy's head — when you fire, it automatically pulls down toward the head.", "Drag your aim downwards and fire upwards: when a shot is fired it auto-levels to the target's headline. For a more stable aim, crouch and shoot.", "The best way to improve aim and accuracy is practice. If you want better headshots, always aim for headshots — it's the only way to practise.", "Sniper rifles give a better chance for swift headshots. In FFF you can choose from SKS, Dragunov, Kar98, AWM, and CG15.", "Adjusting settings, crosshairs, and weapons means nothing without a strategy. Sometimes you need to run or hide quickly to avoid retaliation.").joinToString(sep) }),
            Article("Increase Your Level", "", "\n\n".let { sep -> listOf("EXP points represent game experience. Playing lots of matches in FFF and FFF MAX earns more experience — BR and CS-ranked games give higher EXP.", "Focus on winning, not just participating. Winning maximises the EXP from a match. Note that custom rooms don't reward EXP.", "Complete daily missions to earn more points by playing and winning, plus extra prizes like loadouts and accessories.", "Levelling up costs EXP, so use EXP cards. A card activates automatically at a certain level (100% or 50%) and gives more chances to earn EXP.", "The store sells a 100% EXP card for 100 diamonds — not great for F2P players. Focus on free EXP cards (especially 50% ones) from in-game events and daily guild logins.").joinToString(sep) }),
            Article("Avoid Mistakes", "", "\n\n".let { sep -> listOf("Players often make the mistake of staying still while shooting. It steadies your aim but leaves you more vulnerable to enemy fire.", "Roaming in the open exposes you to fire from all sides. In close-range combat, always use cover or a Gloo Wall for temporary protection.", "Sniper rifles are for long range — they reload after every shot. Using them in close range won't work; the enemy will fire countless bullets by the time you aim.", "Turning your back and running from an enemy is a big mistake — it makes you easy prey and leads to a quick death.", "Close-range fights can cost significant health. Always heal up before engaging in close-range combat to improve your survival odds.").joinToString(sep) }),
            Article("FFF Free Tips", "", "\n\n".let { sep -> listOf("Like other shooters, the high ground wins. Stay on top of buildings and landmarks to shoot down on unaware players — easy cover and an aim advantage.", "FFF has building mechanics: Gloo Walls act as cover mid-fight. Learn tricks like building designs or using them to isolate enemies.", "Stay inside the safe zone — outside it you take damage. Skirt the edge as it moves toward the center to maximise loot, and watch for players doing the same.", "The center of the map is a hotspot and the least efficient place to loot. Start at the edges (or slightly inward) to avoid the swarm.", "Vehicles give great mobility and protection across the map. Learn vehicle locations on each map and get to them — they're a great asset.", "Unlocking Ranked is lenient — you can jump in once you reach level 8. Play standard Battle Royale to level up quickly.", "It's a battle royale, not a race. Don't rush. Drop, grab gear and medkits, and stay hidden. Only fire when required so you don't alert nearby players.", "Spectate from the top. High ground gives a clear view so you can spot and attack enemies before they reach you.", "Keep switching location. Don't stay in one place too long or enemies may find you. Keep progressing and stay in the safe zone.", "Always heal when you get the chance — keep your HP full throughout a match. Look for medkits.", "Use the wide range of characters wisely. Laura and D-bee can improve your accuracy.", "Tune sensitivity settings to improve headshots, and practise to get used to them. Don't copy settings blindly — they vary from player to player.", "For headshots, snipers excel thanks to high damage — a perfect aim can eliminate enemies in one shot. For regular fights, SMGs and assault rifles are best.", "Passive gameplay beats aggressive play by reducing your chance of dying. Survival is the goal — lay low, defend yourself, and strike at the right time.", "Survival first: avoid hot-drop spots. They have great loot but land in less popular spots to avoid dying early.").joinToString(sep) }),
        )
    }
}
